<!-- TRANSIENT — DELETE THIS FILE ONCE FS.GG.UI.Canvas 0.10.0 IS ON THE ORG FEED.

     LIFETIME. The required ApiCompat gate baselines off the PUBLISHED feed, never off the repo's own
     version (ADR-0101's amendment: "the green followed the publish, not the merge"). So a bump to
     0.10.0 does not by itself let a removal merge — vs the published 0.9.0 the members below are gone,
     that is a real CP0002 break, and with `enforce_admins` on (ADR-0103) the red wedges the merge
     button. These two entries are what make the #537 removal executable. Once 0.10.0 publishes, the
     baseline MOVES to it, 0.10.0 does not have these members either, and there is nothing left to
     suppress: delete the file. Same transient, same reason, as the `0.5.0` pair ADR-0104 used to cut
     0.6.0 — and deleted on the day it published.

     NOT A PAPER-OVER. Each entry is `IsBaselineSuppression` and names ONE diagnostic and ONE target, so
     a NEW break introduced later still reddens the gate. The forbidden move is a blanket
     `ApiCompatGenerateSuppressionFile` left in place, which inverts the gate and ships a silent break
     under a preview-patch — the exact failure ADR-0101 registered this gate to prevent.

     WHAT IS SUPPRESSED, AND WHY IT IS DELIBERATE (#537):
       * `Persistence.interpret` — a forwarder to `interpretRecordOnly`, `[<Obsolete>]` since #445.
       * `PersistenceEvidence.#ctor` — the record gained a `Backend` field (#445's type-mark half,
         deferred to the moment a major was already being paid for). Adding a field changes the
         constructor, which is why it could not ship before now. -->

<Suppressions xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <Suppression>
    <DiagnosticId>CP0002</DiagnosticId>
    <Target>M:FS.GG.UI.Canvas.Persistence.interpret(Microsoft.FSharp.Collections.FSharpList{FS.GG.UI.Canvas.PersistenceEffect})</Target>
    <Left>lib/net10.0/FS.GG.UI.Canvas.dll</Left>
    <Right>lib/net10.0/FS.GG.UI.Canvas.dll</Right>
    <IsBaselineSuppression>true</IsBaselineSuppression>
  </Suppression>
  <Suppression>
    <DiagnosticId>CP0002</DiagnosticId>
    <Target>M:FS.GG.UI.Canvas.PersistenceEvidence.#ctor(Microsoft.FSharp.Collections.FSharpList{FS.GG.UI.Canvas.PersistenceEffect})</Target>
    <Left>lib/net10.0/FS.GG.UI.Canvas.dll</Left>
    <Right>lib/net10.0/FS.GG.UI.Canvas.dll</Right>
    <IsBaselineSuppression>true</IsBaselineSuppression>
  </Suppression>
</Suppressions>